<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a null pointer dereference in the `opus_multistream_encoder_init_impl` function in `opus_multistream_encoder.c`. The fuzz driver calls `opus_multistream_encoder_create` with a `NULL` value for the `mapping` parameter. This `NULL` value is then passed down to `opus_multistream_encoder_init_impl`, where it is dereferenced without a null check, causing a segmentation fault.

The project code should be patched to add a null check for the `mapping` parameter in the `opus_multistream_encoder_init_impl` function. If `mapping` is `NULL`, the function should return an error code, such as `OPUS_BAD_ARG`.

A possible patch would be:
```c
--- a/src/opus/src/opus_multistream_encoder.c
+++ b/src/opus/src/opus_multistream_encoder.c
@@ -463,6 +463,8 @@
st->variable_duration = OPUS_FRAMESIZE_ARG;
for (i=0;i<st->layout.nb_channels;i++)
st->layout.mapping[i] = mapping[i];
+   if (mapping == NULL)
+      return OPUS_BAD_ARG;
if (!validate_layout(&st->layout))
return OPUS_BAD_ARG;
if (!validate_encoder_layout(&st->layout))
```
</crash-analysis>

